[[:db/retract 17592186134112 :question/answer-fields 17592186130828] {:db/id 17592186133906 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-6c899a77-435a-5aa3-92d4-0dc3a7b627aa" "question-4e50c9b4-d5fe-527c-b554-c5ae45ba5355"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186134112 :question/problem "$$\nx=\\,{Q}^{T}\\,\n$$\n\nLet $A=QR$  be a QR decomposition of an $m\\times n$ matrix $A$ with linearly independent columns, and the expression above gives the least-squares solution of $Ax=b.$ From left to right, what are the missing parts of the equation?" :question/worked-solution "The least-squares solution of $Ax=b$ satisfies the normal equation\n\n$$\n{A}^{T}Ax={A}^{T}b.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $A=QR,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}Ax & ={A}^{T}b \\\\ (QR)^{T}QRx & =(QR)^{T}b \\\\ {R}^{T}({Q}^{T}Q)Rx & ={R}^{T}{Q}^{T}b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $Q$ has orthonormal columns, ${Q}^{T}Q=I,$ and we get\n\n$$\n{R}^{T}Rx={R}^{T}\\,{Q}^{T}b.\n$$\n\nThen, since ${R}^{T}$ is invertible, pre-multiplying by $({R}^{T})^{-1}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({R}^{T})^{-1}\\cdot {R}^{T}Rx & =({R}^{T})^{-1}\\cdot {R}^{T}{Q}^{T}b \\\\ Rx & ={Q}^{T}b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since $R$ is invertible, pre-multiplying by ${R}^{-1}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}^{-1}\\cdot Rx & ={R}^{-1}\\cdot {Q}^{T}b \\\\ x & ={R}^{-1}\\,\\,{Q}^{T}\\,\\,b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing parts of the equation are ${R}^{-1}$ and $b.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-6d57014e-b23a-5701-a76a-a3703de7149c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6d57014e-b23a-5701-a76a-a3703de7149c" :answer-field/id #uuid "6d57014e-b23a-5701-a76a-a3703de7149c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-0acc060c-c80f-5318-9ceb-31102a3b5205" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d56e2344-c38a-5d60-89d9-ddd844e5f790" "answer-05f55e0b-2bfd-5324-bb60-ef44a8ce8695" "answer-accbb9fd-1e2b-5eb4-9d55-1c270308aa87" "answer-0acc060c-c80f-5318-9ceb-31102a3b5205" "answer-e8d265c7-1332-5802-b568-b47af3ef47f8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d56e2344-c38a-5d60-89d9-ddd844e5f790" :answer/id #uuid "d56e2344-c38a-5d60-89d9-ddd844e5f790" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$R$ and $b$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-05f55e0b-2bfd-5324-bb60-ef44a8ce8695" :answer/id #uuid "05f55e0b-2bfd-5324-bb60-ef44a8ce8695" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$R$ and ${b}^{T}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-accbb9fd-1e2b-5eb4-9d55-1c270308aa87" :answer/id #uuid "accbb9fd-1e2b-5eb4-9d55-1c270308aa87" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${R}^{-1}$ and $A$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0acc060c-c80f-5318-9ceb-31102a3b5205" :answer/id #uuid "0acc060c-c80f-5318-9ceb-31102a3b5205" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${R}^{-1}$ and $b$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e8d265c7-1332-5802-b568-b47af3ef47f8" :answer/id #uuid "e8d265c7-1332-5802-b568-b47af3ef47f8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${R}^{T}$ and $b$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133803 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-c8892a71-2970-5d65-891c-76f1124825ea" "question-6e2326cd-c939-5766-9e1e-50b935159886"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-c8892a71-2970-5d65-891c-76f1124825ea" :question/id #uuid "c8892a71-2970-5d65-891c-76f1124825ea" :question/math-academy-id "q-139796" :question/problem "Given the QR decomposition $A=QR,$ find the least-squares solution to $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nQ=\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{2} & -1 \\\\ 2\\sqrt{2} & -1 \\\\ \\sqrt{2} & 4\\end{aligned}],\\,R=\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}3\\sqrt{2} & -4\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The least-squares solution of $Ax=b$ satisfies the corresponding normal equation:\n\n$$\n{A}^{T}Ax={A}^{T}b\n$$\n\nSubstituting $A=QR,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}Ax & ={A}^{T}b \\\\ (QR)^{T}QRx & =(QR)^{T}b \\\\ {R}^{T}({Q}^{T}Q)Rx & ={R}^{T}{Q}^{T}b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $Q$ has orthonormal columns, ${Q}^{T}Q=I,$ and we get\n\n$$\n{R}^{T}Rx={R}^{T}\\,{Q}^{T}b.\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${R}^{T}$ is invertible, pre-multiplying by $({R}^{T})^{-1}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({R}^{T})^{-1}\\cdot {R}^{T}Rx & =({R}^{T})^{-1}\\cdot {R}^{T}{Q}^{T}b \\\\ Rx & ={Q}^{T}b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting our matrices, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{R}{\\overset{⏞}{\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}3\\sqrt{2} & -4\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]}}x & =\\overset{{Q}^{T}}{\\overset{⏞}{\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{2} & 2\\sqrt{2} & \\sqrt{2} \\\\ -1 & -1 & 4\\end{aligned}]}}\\overset{b}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]}} \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}3\\sqrt{2} & -4\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]x & =[\\begin{aligned}38\\sqrt{2} \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3\\sqrt{2}{x}_{1}-4\\sqrt{2}{x}_{2}=38\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 2{x}_{2}=-10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=-5.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\sqrt{2}{x}_{1}-4\\sqrt{2}(-5) & =38\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 3\\sqrt{2}{x}_{1} & =18\\sqrt{2} \\\\ {x}_{1} & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the least-squares solution to $Ax=b$ is $[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}].$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-44672c62-c008-5400-a940-292eccf518a4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-44672c62-c008-5400-a940-292eccf518a4" :answer-field/id #uuid "44672c62-c008-5400-a940-292eccf518a4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-ab331c8e-8ec8-5a70-b8c2-e3efcd32bf48" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0cfa9745-27c9-5c69-9259-9f33cdd30cbd" "answer-84becdeb-7cb6-51f9-8247-37058f839cfa" "answer-290a80b2-d833-5e18-ba11-922da75fadbb" "answer-ab331c8e-8ec8-5a70-b8c2-e3efcd32bf48" "answer-d9a2f5a3-da1b-5892-8fa1-25b99c4d869f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0cfa9745-27c9-5c69-9259-9f33cdd30cbd" :answer/id #uuid "0cfa9745-27c9-5c69-9259-9f33cdd30cbd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-84becdeb-7cb6-51f9-8247-37058f839cfa" :answer/id #uuid "84becdeb-7cb6-51f9-8247-37058f839cfa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-290a80b2-d833-5e18-ba11-922da75fadbb" :answer/id #uuid "290a80b2-d833-5e18-ba11-922da75fadbb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ab331c8e-8ec8-5a70-b8c2-e3efcd32bf48" :answer/id #uuid "ab331c8e-8ec8-5a70-b8c2-e3efcd32bf48" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d9a2f5a3-da1b-5892-8fa1-25b99c4d869f" :answer/id #uuid "d9a2f5a3-da1b-5892-8fa1-25b99c4d869f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-6e2326cd-c939-5766-9e1e-50b935159886" :question/id #uuid "6e2326cd-c939-5766-9e1e-50b935159886" :question/math-academy-id "q-157095" :question/problem "Given the QR decomposition $A=QR,$ find the least-squares solution to $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nQ=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{42}}[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{14} & 2\\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\sqrt{14} & -3\\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\sqrt{14} & \\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,R=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{42}}[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{14} & 3\\sqrt{14} \\\\ 0 & 3\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The least-squares solution of $Ax=b$ satisfies the corresponding normal equation:\n\n$$\n{A}^{T}Ax={A}^{T}b\n$$\n\nSubstituting $A=QR,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}Ax & ={A}^{T}b \\\\ (QR)^{T}QRx & =(QR)^{T}b \\\\ {R}^{T}({Q}^{T}Q)Rx & ={R}^{T}{Q}^{T}b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $Q$ has orthonormal columns, ${Q}^{T}Q=I,$ and we get\n\n$$\n{R}^{T}Rx={R}^{T}\\,{Q}^{T}b.\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${R}^{T}$ is invertible, pre-multiplying by $({R}^{T})^{-1}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({R}^{T})^{-1}\\cdot {R}^{T}Rx & =({R}^{T})^{-1}\\cdot {R}^{T}{Q}^{T}b \\\\ Rx & ={Q}^{T}b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting our matrices, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{R}{\\overset{⏞}{\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{42}}[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{14} & 3\\sqrt{14} \\\\ 0 & 3\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}]}}x & =\\overset{{Q}^{T}}{\\overset{⏞}{\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{42}}[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{14} & \\sqrt{14} & \\sqrt{14} \\\\ 2\\sqrt{3} & -3\\sqrt{3} & \\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}]}}\\overset{b}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]}} \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{14} & 3\\sqrt{14} \\\\ 0 & 3\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}]x & =[\\begin{aligned}-3\\sqrt{14} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{14}{x}_{1}+3\\sqrt{14}{x}_{2}=-3\\sqrt{14} \\\\ 3\\sqrt{3}{x}_{2}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=0.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{14}{x}_{1}+3\\sqrt{14}(0) & =-3\\sqrt{14} \\\\ \\sqrt{14}{x}_{1} & =-3\\sqrt{14} \\\\ {x}_{1} & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the least-squares solution to $Ax=b$ is $[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8a8d53f7-b5fc-5ce6-9a9c-54a7385b4356"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8a8d53f7-b5fc-5ce6-9a9c-54a7385b4356" :answer-field/id #uuid "8a8d53f7-b5fc-5ce6-9a9c-54a7385b4356" :answe